# Old-domain redirect for a domain migration (docs/runbooks/domain-migration.md).
# Copy to old-domain.caddy, replace the hostname, `docker compose up -d`.
#
# The old name listens on the same PUBLIC_PORT (the only published port) and
# gets its certificate the same way as the main site — `tls_dns` is the
# DNS-01 snippet from the main Caddyfile (Caddyfile.local defines the same
# name as `tls internal`, so this block also works in local rehearsals). Both
# names must be in the zone the API token can edit.
#
# `redir ... {uri} 308` forwards the full path AND query string, so every
# previously shared https://old-host:PORT/s/<id> link lands on the same
# capture at the new host; 308 (not 301/302) keeps the method for API
# clients. Caddy manages a certificate for this name as long as the block
# exists and DNS for it still points here — remove the block only when you
# are ready for old links to stop working (see the runbook's redirect-lifetime
# section).
old.shots.example.com:{$PUBLIC_PORT} {
	import tls_dns
	redir https://{$PUBLIC_HOST}:{$PUBLIC_PORT}{uri} 308
}
